Package: liblibrescrs5
Architecture: amd64
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: librescrs-card-plugins (= ${binary:Version})
Description: LibreSCRS smart-card runtime libraries
 LibreSCRS reads Serbian government smart cards (identity, vehicle and health)
 as well as ICAO 9303 travel documents, NIST PIV and PKCS#15 cards, talking
 to the reader over PC/SC directly.
 .
 This package holds the shared libraries and the PKCS#11 provider module. The
 module is installed but not registered with p11-kit; registration is a
 separate decision and a separate package.

Package: librescrs-card-plugins
Architecture: amd64
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, liblibrescrs5 (= ${binary:Version})
Description: Card plugins for the LibreSCRS smart-card libraries
 One plugin per card family, loaded at run time, with the manifest that
 describes the fields each one exposes.
 .
 Without this package the libraries load and enumerate readers but recognize
 no card.

Package: liblibrescrs-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: amd64
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         liblibrescrs5 (= ${binary:Version}),
         libpcsclite-dev,
         libssl-dev
Description: Development files for the LibreSCRS smart-card libraries
 Headers, linker symbolic links and the CMake package configuration for
 building against LibreSCRS.
 .
 The two development dependencies are not decoration. The installed CMake
 config calls find_dependency for PCSC and for OpenSSL before it defines a
 single target, so without their headers every downstream find_package fails at
 configuration -- which is exactly how it was found.
